  "decision": "NO_CHANGE",
  "workflow_yaml": null,
  "rationale": "The workflow already implements the supported optimizations that fit it: dependency caching is present via Swatinem/rust-cache (P-LIT-GHA-CACHE), every job already has an explicit timeout-minutes (P-LIT-CUSTOM-TIMEOUT), and concurrency with cancel-in-progress for non-main refs already supersedes stale runs (P-LIT-CANCEL-STALE). The remaining candidate, P-LIT-FAIL-FAST (setting fail-fast: true on the test matrix), is contraindicated here: the matrix spans ubuntu/macos/windows and every matrix outcome is part of the intended cross-platform test coverage, so cancelling remaining jobs after a failure would reduce required-check coverage rather than preserve it. No supported, minimal, coverage-preserving change remains.",
  "evidence_ids": ["P-LIT-GHA-CACHE", "P-LIT-CUSTOM-TIMEOUT", "P-LIT-CANCEL-STALE", "P-LIT-FAIL-FAST"]
}
